<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Richard Seddon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1845">1845</a>–<a href="/years/1906">1906</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as King Dick</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Richard Seddon was an English-born politician and the longest-serving prime minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a>, in office from 1893 until his death in 1906. Leading the Liberal government, he oversaw <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/social-insurance">old-age pensions</a>, compulsory labour arbitration and land reform. He was a strong supporter of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> and sent New Zealand troops to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-boer-war">Second Boer War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/richard-seddon.jpg" alt="Richard Seddon" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Herman John Schmidt · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Richard_Seddon_portrait_1905.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1897 Premier <b>Richard Seddon</b> presented a copy of the words and music to Queen Victoria.</blockquote><a href="/songs/god-defend-new-zealand">God Defend New Zealand</a></li><li><blockquote>The Liberal Party won; <b>Richard Seddon</b> became prime minister.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/november-28">28 November in history</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Richard Seddon's</b> Liberal government, in office from 1893, pioneered old-age pensions, compulsory labour arbitration and the purchase of large estates for small farmers.</blockquote><a href="/state/colony-of-new-zealand">Colony of New Zealand</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Richard Seddon's</b> New Zealand government sought to expand in the Pacific.</blockquote><a href="/state/cook-islands-federation">Cook Islands Federation</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Eccleston, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-kingdom">the United Kingdom</a>. Died in Tasman Sea. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=53.45,-2.78&amp;year=1884" aria-label="Eccleston on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4488 326 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Richard Seddon"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4938 596h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4938 596h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=53.45,-2.78&amp;year=1884">What was here in 1884? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
